# --- Python (backend) ---
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.egg-info/
.venv
venv
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
*.db
# SQLite writes two sidecars beside the database in WAL mode, and a third in
# rollback-journal mode. `*.db` matches none of them, which is how a local
# database's write-ahead log came to be tracked: it changes on every run, so it
# dirtied every working tree and was swept into commits by anything using
# `git add -A`.
*.db-shm
*.db-wal
*.db-journal
*.sqlite*
# `*.db` does not match a backup copy either, because the timestamp lands after
# the extension - which is how `backend/sketchy.db.broken-20260827-033005`, a
# whole database with a signing secret in it, reached a public remote. Twice now
# this list has only covered the shapes someone had already thought of, so
# `scripts/check-tracked-artifacts.sh` refuses anything whose *bytes* are a
# SQLite database, under any name at all.
*.db.*

